🏴‍☠️🇺🇸⚔️🇱🇧 The enemy army has begun withdrawing a number of its forces from the town of Debbine. The municipality of Marjayoun received a call from the Israeli army stating that the road between Marjayoun and Hasbaya is now open, but it urged citizens not to use it pending an official statement from the Lebanese Army Command. The Lebanese Army has begun reopening the Marjayoun–Debbine–Ebel El Saqi road following the Israeli withdrawal.

All of these villages and towns are historically known as Christian and Druze villages. We are happy for the residents of these towns, but was that part of the deal nobody mentioned in the statement? Does the "President" didn't care about the other villages? 

@stayfreeworld

ICYMI: A railcar carrying lithium batteries caught fire in the Cajon Pass overnight, prompting a response from San Bernardino County firefighters and hazardous materials crews. Railway officials say that the blaze started while it was being burglarized. 

At around 3:45 a.m., San Bernardino County Fire Department officials posted on social media , saying that the single BNSF railcar “loaded with lithium batteries” was well involved with fire on the tracks near Swarthout Canyon in an area that was difficult to access for crews.

@police_frequency

